## Command Notes

- Do not use `kubectl run -it ... --rm` or `kubectl exec -it ...` in this autonomous, non-interactive session. Interactive attach can hang after the pod completes, especially when piped through commands like `head`.
- For temporary curl/debug pods, use non-interactive commands with deterministic pod names, `timeout`, and explicit cleanup:
  ```bash
  kubectl run curl-test -n {{ namespace }} --restart=Never --image=curlimages/curl:latest --command -- curl -fsS http://frontend:5000/
  kubectl delete pod curl-test -n {{ namespace }} --ignore-not-found
  ```
- When possible, prefer `kubectl exec` without `-i` or `-t`, for example `kubectl exec -n {{ namespace }} deploy/frontend -- wget -qO- http://localhost:5000/`.
